<section class="about-section" id="experience"><h2>Experience</h2>
<article class="timeline"><time>2026</time><div><h3>AI comics &amp; storyboard automation</h3><p class="role">System design &amp; development · Script to storyboard</p><p>Built a storyboard automation system from the ground up, connecting script parsing, narrative timelines, scene analysis, and shot generation. Extended it to reuse character, scene, and prop assets across episodes, with task scheduling and quality evaluation to carry creative context forward.</p><details><summary>Explore the work</summary><ul><li>Built a staged script-to-storyboard workflow, checking source coverage and binding shots to specific characters and scenes.</li><li>Implemented rolling execution across episodes, managing shared identities and assets with stage-level caching to reduce repeated computation.</li><li>Built API services and dependency-based scheduling. Used a fixed evaluation set to assess character matching, scene consistency, and shot continuity, then refine generation rules.</li></ul></details></div></article>
<article class="timeline"><time>2025–2026</time><div><h3>Cross-episode character identity</h3><p class="role">Identity modeling · Editing integration</p><p>Built an identity alignment workflow for short-drama editing, addressing characters being recognized as different people across episodes. Connected within-episode grouping, persistent identities, and video understanding to the editing pipeline so footage could be organized around consistent character threads.</p><details><summary>Explore the work</summary><ul><li>Linked within-episode character groups to a shared identity library, using stable identifiers to connect appearances and reduce ambiguity from names or visual descriptions alone.</li><li>Aligned character entities from video understanding with identity results, and designed rules for aliases, unknown identities, semantic conflicts, and manual correction.</li><li>Integrated the standalone identity service into the editing workflow, improving interfaces, concurrent scheduling, cache reuse, and identity-disambiguation performance.</li></ul></details></div></article>
<article class="timeline"><time>2024</time><div><h3>Enterprise RAG &amp; safety review</h3><p class="role">Core algorithm engineering</p><p>Worked on enterprise document retrieval and internal safety review, using hierarchical chunking, multi-stage retrieval, and dynamic thresholds, with prompts to support review.</p><details><summary>Explore the work</summary><ul><li>Hierarchical chunking, multi-stage retrieval, and dynamic thresholds.</li><li>Prompt-assisted workflows for internal safety review.</li></ul></details></div></article>
</section>
